# Auto commit with change details

When a task changes files, commit that work before you stop. Do not wait to be asked again.

## When to commit

- Commit once the task is done and the related files are saved.
- One task, one commit. Keep unrelated edits out of the same commit.
- Skip secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens) and warn if they were requested.
- Do not create an empty commit.
- Do not push unless the user asks.

## Commit message

`.cursor/hooks/auto-commit.sh` commits through `scripts/commit_message.py`. That script must write a specific title plus bullets. A title that is only `Update <filename>` is not acceptable.

```
Keep a full-page receipt upright instead of cropping one table

- scan_document.py: def _content_fills_frame
- scan_document.py: skip the crop when the page already fills the photo
```

The title says what behavior changed. Each bullet names the file and the function, comment, or line that changed. Do not stop at the filename.
